.TH GIT-HUNK 1 "2026-08-21" "hunkyard" "Git Manual"
.SH NAME
git-hunk \- review code changes from a local repository or a pull request
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git hunk
[\fItarget\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B git hunk status
.br
.B git hunk stop
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens a review of local changes, a branch, or a GitHub pull request in your
browser.
.PP
The server runs in the background and serves every repository you have opened,
so running
.B hunk
in a second repository does not need it restarted. It keeps running until you
stop it.
.PP
.B git hunk
and
.B hunk
are the same executable; the installer links both names.
.SH TARGETS
.TP
(none)
Unstaged changes in the working tree.
.TP
.B \-\-staged
Staged changes only.
.TP
.B \-\-all
Staged and unstaged together.
.TP
.I revspec
A range or revision, such as
.IR main...feature ,
.IR HEAD~3 ,
.IR a1b2c3d ,
or
.IR v1.0...v2.0 .
A three-dot range is diffed against the merge base, the same anchor GitHub uses
for a pull request, so line numbers agree with the eventual PR.
.TP
.I owner/repo#123
A GitHub pull request.
.TP
.I url
A github.com pull request, commit or compare URL.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show the running server and the repositories it serves.
.TP
.B stop
Stop the running server.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " " \fIn\fR
Port to serve on. Defaults to 4865.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-open
Print the URL instead of opening a browser.
.TP
.B \-\-foreground
Hold the terminal instead of running in the background.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the short help.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .hunkyard/review.md
Review threads for a local target, written in the repository being reviewed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GH_TOKEN
.TQ
.B GITHUB_TOKEN
A GitHub token for pull requests. Read from
.B gh auth token
when neither is set. Only private pull requests need one. It stays in the server
process and is never handed to the browser.
.SH EXAMPLES
Review what you have not committed:
.PP
.RS
.B git hunk
.RE
.PP
Review a branch the way its pull request will show it:
.PP
.RS
.B git hunk main...my\-branch
.RE
.PP
Review a pull request:
.PP
.RS
.B git hunk owner/repo#123
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-diff (1),
.BR git-range-diff (1)
